OPTIMISER OPTIMISATIONS:

  * JOIN ORDER
  * REPLACE SCAN BY INDEXSCAN WHERE INDEX EXISTS ON FILTER COLUMNS.
  * WHEN ORDERED DATA BEING AGGREGATED CHANGE AGGREG TO ORDAGGREG
    REMOVING ALL SUBSEQUENT NODE AND ORIGIN LEVEL AGGREGATES
  * ORDER BY (SORT) CAN BE DISCARDED WHEN IT IS ON THE SAME COLUMNS AS GROUP BY
  * LITERAL ARITHMETIC UPFRONT
  * FILTER PUSH-DOWN
  * MINIMIZING PROJECTION AS EARLY AS POSSIBLE
  * FILTERS FROM OUTER-QUERY TO BE PULLED INTO INNER-QUERY
  * DELAY GETTING VARCHAR COLUMNS EVEN IF MEANS JOIN AGAIN
  * SOMETIMES ADDED A SORT TO CHANGE AN AGGREG TO AN ORDAGG
    REMOVING ALL SUBSEQUENT NODE AND ORIGIN LEVEL AGGREGATES
  * IF THERE IS A SORT AFTER AN AGGREG THEN PLANNER GENERATES ONLY ON ORIGIN
    SO IF WE CHANGE AGGREG TO ORDAGG WE CAN INTRODUCE SORT+LIMIT AT ALL 3 LEVELS TO
    TO REDUCE DATA EARLY.
  * DERIVE FILTERS AND PUSH-DOWN (eg QUERY7 & QUERY19)
  * DROP ALL OTHER GROUP BY KEYS IF ONE OF THEM IS KNOWN TO BE UNIQUE.
  * REPLACE SORT SORTOP DESC + LIMITOP BY TOPOP (WITH LIMIT AS PARAMETER TO IT))
  * CHANGE FILTER ORDER DEPENDING ON SELECTION (MIN TO MAX)
    ... NOT SURE HOW OPTIMIZER CAN FIGURE THIS OUT.
